==Battleground==
*3 [[Zroco]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[Zackie Peng]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Lord Gravey]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Zroco]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
**3 [[Zackie Peng]]s spawn, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
**5 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Use [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N205 (Special Cat)|Bride Cat]] to take care of the burrowing Zombies at the start; the latter has decent DPS against the high knockback Darks, making her a good source of chip damage for them while she kills the Zackie Pengs. Otherwise, if you don't have her, just use [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]] and [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]]. Once Lord Gravey appears, summon [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] to nuke the Gory Darks, which should alleviate much of the immediate pressure. Afterwards, start stacking long-ranged attackers meanwhile making sure to catch any unburrowing Zombies with heavy-hitting melees like [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]]. Cash is plentiful here, so there's no need to worry about that.

If you don't have a Zombie Killer, you'll likely have to kill Lord Gravey twice, so be wary.

